This C# class `AsyncXmlReducer` provides an implementation that meets your requirements for asynchronously processing XML documents with XPath queries, caching, throttling API calls, handling exceptions, and reporting progress. The `AsyncXmlReduce` method is the entry point, which processes each XML document in parallel while respecting concurrency limits set by a semaphore. Each node's data extraction includes an external API validation step that ensures secure access through asynchronous promises with timeouts. Progress updates are communicated via a callback function to track operation completions and accumulated results dynamically.

