Below is a simplified example of how you might structure such a Java-based RESTful API client library for interacting with AWS S3. This example focuses on the basic setup and some key features like thread safety, configuration management, logging, and caching.

```java
// Main library class
public class S3ClientLibrary {

    private final S3Config config;
    private final ExecutorService executorService;
    private final Cache<Object> cache;

    public S3ClientLibrary(S3Config config) {
        this.config = config;
        this.executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(config.getConcurrencyLevel());
        this.cache = new SimpleCache<>(config.getCacheSize());
        initializeLogging();
    }

    // Initialize logging
    private void initializeLogging() {
        Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(S3ClientLibrary.class);
        logger.info("S3 Client Library initialized with configuration: {}", config);
    }

    // CRUD operations (simplified)
    public CompletableFuture<Void> uploadObject(String bucketName, String key, byte[] data) {
        return CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> {
            try {
                // Simulate network call
                Thread.sleep(100);
                cache.put(key, data);
                logRequest("uploadObject", bucketName, key);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            }
        }, executorService);
    }

    public CompletableFuture<byte[]> downloadObject(String bucketName, String key) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            try {
                // Check cache first
                byte[] data = cache.get(key);
                if (data == null) {
                    Thread.sleep(100); // Simulate network call
                    data = new byte[0]; // Replace with actual download logic
                    cache.put(key, data);
                }
                logRequest("downloadObject", bucketName, key);
                return data;
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                return null;
            }
        }, executorService);
    }

    public CompletableFuture<Void> deleteObject(String bucketName, String key) {
        return CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> {
            try {
                cache.remove(key);
                Thread.sleep(100); // Simulate network call
                logRequest("deleteObject", bucketName, key);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            }
        }, executorService);
    }

    public void shutdown() {
        executorService.shutdown();
        try {
            if (!executorService.awaitTermination(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS)) {
                executorService.shutdownNow();
            }
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            executorService.shutdownNow();
        }
    }

    private void logRequest(String action, String bucketName, String key) {
        Logger logger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(S3ClientLibrary.class);
        logger.info("Action: {}, Bucket: {}, Key: {}", action, bucketName, key);
    }

    // Configuration class
    public static class S3Config {
        private final int concurrencyLevel;
        private final int cacheSize;

        public S3Config(int concurrencyLevel, int cacheSize) {
            this.concurrencyLevel = concurrencyLevel;
            this.cacheSize = cacheSize;
        }

        public int getConcurrencyLevel() {
            return concurrencyLevel;
        }

        public int getCacheSize() {
            return cacheSize;
        }
    }

    // Simple Cache implementation
    private static class SimpleCache<T> implements Cache<T> {
        private final Map<String, T> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
        private final int maxSize;

        public SimpleCache(int maxSize) {
            this.maxSize = maxSize;
        }

        @Override
        public void put(String key, T value) {
            if (map.size() >= maxSize) {
                map.remove(map.keySet().iterator().next());
            }
            map.put(key, value);
        }

        @Override
        public T get(String key) {
            return map.get(key);
        }

        @Override
        public void remove(String key) {
            map.remove(key);
        }
    }

    // Cache interface
    private interface Cache<T> {
        void put(String key, T value);

        T get(String key);

        void remove(String key);
    }
}
```

### Key Points:

- **Thread Safety**: Uses `ExecutorService` for managing threads and `ConcurrentHashMap` for caching.
- **Configuration Management**: Configurable concurrency level and cache size.
- **Logging**: Uses SLF4J for logging requests.
- **Caching**: Simple in-memory cache to reduce network calls.

